## Reading These Docs

- Script steps are shown as FileMaker's Script Workspace prints them. `{ also: … }` after a step holds parameters FileMaker's own text leaves out.
- Privileges: each privilege set page lists its custom access. Script, layout, value list and field pages have an "Access by Privilege Set" table when any set restricts them individually.
- An empty "Called By" doesn't mean a script is unused. Other files, server schedules, `fmp://` URLs and Perform Script by name don't show up here.
- {% if coverage.available %}[Reports/coverage.md](Reports/coverage.md) compares{% else %}A `--coverage` build compares{% endif %} what's in the XML with what reached these pages. Don't rely on an area it marks as short.
- `[REDACTED:…]` marks a value that scrubbing replaced. The text around it isn't the file's real code.

